wikipedia_extract: 'Three naval vessels of Japan have been named Makigumo (巻雲), meaning
  "Cirrus Clouds" (Rolling Clouds).[1]


  Japanese destroyer Makigumo (1905) was a Shikinami-class destroyer in the Imperial
  Japanese Navy. Originally, she was a Kazarsky-class torpedo cruiser Vsadnik of the
  Imperial Russian Navy.

  Japanese destroyer Makigumo (1941) was a Yūgumo-class destroyer in the Imperial
  Japanese Navy. She was completed in 1942, scuttled in 1943, and struck in 1943.

  JDS Makigumo (DD-114) was a Yamagumo-class destroyer in the Japanese Maritime Self-Defense
  Force. She was launched in 1967 and decommissioned in 1995.'
